From fe59ba12dd1d76e14545cf7cb563d70c990ba24f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:32:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DongleAtCommand: AMI action with correlated
 DongleAtResponse/DongleAtDone events

Upstream: https://github.com/wdoekes/asterisk-chan-dongle @ 31eb619600d5ce93237cd440c72db0bc33d7adfe
Purpose: DongleAtCommand action + DongleAtResponse/DongleAtDone events for Aster
         (protocol contract: docker/asterisk/patches/README.md in the Aster repository)

An AMI client sends one AT command to a device and receives the modem's answer through events
that carry the action's ActionID. Lines are attributed by the driver's own command queue, never
by timing:

- at_queue: a task carries the ActionID of the DongleAtCommand that queued it (empty for every
  other task). at_queue_insert_actionid() sets the tag only after the command was written, so an
  action that fails with "Queue error" never produces an event. at_queue_actionid_done() emits
  the single DongleAtDone of the head task and clears the tag, so nothing later is attributed to
  that ActionID. at_queue_flush() (disconnect, reset, restart) ends tagged tasks with
  Result: ERROR, Error: queue flushed; a tagged task removed for any other reason gets
  Error: task removed.
- at_command: at_enqueue_user_cmd_id() queues a CMD_USER task with the action's timeout, ahead
  of other pending commands, exactly like the "dongle cmd" CLI command does.
- at_response: for a tagged CMD_USER task every line that is neither the final result nor an
  unsolicited report (^RSSI, ^MODE, RING, ^CEND, +CMTI, ...) is a DongleAtResponse; OK ends the
  task with Result: OK, ERROR / +CMS ERROR / +CME ERROR with Result: ERROR and the line as
  Error. "+CME ERROR:" is added to the response table so that it is handled like "+CMS ERROR:"
  instead of being ignored until the command times out.
- chan_dongle do_monitor_phone(): a response timeout emits Result: TIMEOUT before the existing
  handling disconnects and restarts the device.
- manager: the DongleAtCommand action (EVENT_FLAG_SYSTEM) validates ActionID (1-63 characters
  [A-Za-z0-9._-]), Command (1-256 characters, no CR/LF) and Timeout (1-60 s, default 15) before
  the device lookup, then requires the device to be connected and initialized. The events escape
  CR/LF like manager_event_message().

Untagged user commands (CLI "dongle cmd") behave as before and emit nothing.
